-**No `Array(...)` wrapper is needed on Swift 6.1+.** As of Swift 6.1, the sequence returned by `.enumerated()` conditionally conforms to `RandomAccessCollection` when the base collection does, so `ForEach` accepts it directly. On earlier toolchains, wrap it in `Array(...)`. Favor the direct form in new code — it avoids an eager copy on every body evaluation.
+**No `Array(...)` wrapper is needed with Swift 6.2 and an iOS 26 / macOS 26 / tvOS 26 / watchOS 26 / visionOS 26 deployment target.** SE-0459 makes the sequence returned by `.enumerated()` conditionally conform to `RandomAccessCollection` when the base collection does, so `ForEach` accepts it directly. For earlier toolchains or targets, wrap it in `Array(...)`. Favor the direct form in new code; it avoids an eager copy on every body evaluation.
 
